The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/weather/weather-05-triangular-resampling-footgun.md`.

**Quick summary of findings:**

| Severity | Count | Key points |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| Medium | 1 | EnergyPlus uses the same non-conservative triangular scheme as its **mandatory** default with zero warnings, normalising an unsafe practice for migrating users |
| Low | 2 | (1) `ResampleOverrides` has no runtime warning when solar fields are set to `Triangular`; (2) legitimate use cases exist (E+ parity, high-res control modelling, transient comfort) that justify keeping the method as opt-in |

**Recommendation**: Keep `Triangular`, but strengthen the guardrails — add a `tracing::warn!` in `resample_with` when any solar override is `Triangular`, add docstrings to `ResampleOverrides`, and document EnergyPlus's equivalent non-conservation in the `Triangular` variant's own docstring so users coming from E+ understand that HARES's ZOH default is the architecturally superior choice.
